{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgrqv9FBmn7R1XxMUYUWG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012PDt4BSymmGVSc6bKs75dc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p .nightralph; cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 01 notes\n\n## Item 1: assembled parts == render\n- render-support: `renderParts(rec, props, options)` returns { tag, attrs, html };\n  `renderHost` now builds its string from the parts. Registered under\n  `Symbol.for('microtags.renderParts')` beside `microtags.render`.\n- attrs built as pairs -> Object.fromEntries so a `__proto__` key from\n  data stays an own property. Duplicate names (declared prop and extra\n  attr with the same name) keep the first value. Before, the string held\n  both; an HTML parser keeps the first, so the parsed result is the same,\n  but bytes differ in that one edge case (no existing test covered it).\n- core: one `link(key)` helper builds both statics.\n- test/ssr.ts: `assembleParts` helper + PartsEl fixture with every prop kind.\nEOF\ngit add -A src test && git commit -qm \"Add renderParts static and render-support parts function\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && echo done"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":220,"cache_read_input_tokens":78856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":220},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b761de01-256c-46ce-80ea-a1724a155a95","uuid":"5ac71f2d-c001-4ef2-acd0-6349a4a95886","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:00:31.632Z","request_id":"req_011Cgrqv93XuHj3M5RRf9JX9","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012PDt4BSymmGVSc6bKs75dc":{"command":"mkdir -p .nightralph; cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 01 notes\n\n## Item 1: assembled parts == render\n- render-support: `renderParts(rec, props, options)` returns { tag, attrs, html };\n  `renderHost` now builds its string from the parts. Registered under\n  `Symbol.for('microtags.renderParts')` beside `microtags.render`.\n- attrs built as pairs -> Object.fromEntries so a `__proto__` key from\n  data stays an own property. Duplicate names (declared prop and extra\n  attr with the same name) keep the first value. Before, the string held\n  both; an HTML parser keeps the first, so the parsed result is the same,\n  but bytes differ in that one edge case (no existing test covered it).\n- core: one `link(key)` helper builds both statics.\n- test/ssr.ts: `assembleParts` helper + PartsEl fixture with every prop kind.\nEOF\ngit add -A src test && git commit -qm \"Add renderParts static and render-support parts function\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && echo done"}}}
