{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JdCrGfdPgWC2VC1aJHwWdd","type":"tool_result","content":"### `builder.render(fn, options?)`\n\nAttach a render function that produces the component's inner HTML as a\nstring. The render function receives a context with `props` (plain\nresolved values, not signals), `refs`, `TAG`, `children` (inner HTML\nfrom the caller), and `attrs` (extra attributes from the caller).\n\n```ts\ndefine('my-counter')\n    .withProps(p => ({\n        start: p.number(),\n    }))\n    .withRefs(r => ({\n        display: r.one<HTMLDivElement>(),\n        inc: r.one(),\n        dec: r.one(),\n    }))\n    .render(({ props, refs }) => {\n        return `\n            <div data-ref=\"${refs.display}\">\n                ${props.start}\n            </div>\n            <button data-ref=\"${refs.dec}\">-</button>\n            <button data-ref=\"${refs.inc}\">+</button>\n        `\n    })\n    .setup(ctx => {\n        // hydration code only\n    })\n```\n\nThe returned element class gains two statics: `render(props, options?)`\nwhich returns complete host markup, and `props`, the list of declared\nprop names. `options` accepts `children` (a string of inner HTML) and\n`attrs` (an object of extra attributes, all strings).\n\n`props` are the names declared in `.withProps`. They are serialized onto\nthe host tag with the prop's serializer, so `.setup` can coerce them back\non the client. `attrs` are any other attributes the caller put on the\ntag, such as `class`, `id`, or `aria-*`. They are written to the host tag\nas-is, and are available to the render function so it can forward them\ninside. See [Hydration](#hydration) for an example.\n\nThe static `render` needs the server render support module, which\nbuilds the host tag and serializes props. The `microtags/htm`\ntemplater loads it, on the server and in the browser. Code that calls\na component's `render` static directly, without the templater, must\nimport [`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support) once.\nWithout it, `render` throws an error naming that module.\n\n```ts\nimport 'microtags/render-support'\nimport { MyCounter } from './components.js'\n\nconst markup = MyCounter.render({ start: 5 })\n```\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> This is a breaking change in 0.0.x. Before it, `render` worked with\n> no extra import.\n\nPass `{ client: true }` to keep the render function in the client\nbundle after [`microbuild`](#microbuild) strips it:\n\n```ts\n.render(renderFn, { client: true })\n```\n\nSee [`client:true` vs `--keep`](#clienttrue-vs---keep) for when to\nuse each.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> `.render` on the builder is unrelated to\n> [`microtags/render`](#microtagsrender), which is a DOM reconciler\n> for lists and single items.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n### `builder.setup(ctx)`\n\nRegisters the custom element via `customElements.define` and returns the\nelement class. The returned class exposes `.TAG` and `.refs` as static\nmembers, for use in [serverside rendering](#serverside-example).\n\n```ts\nclass ComponentBuilder {\n    setup (\n        fn:(ctx:SetupContext<\n            Props,\n            RefsMap<RefDefs>,\n            ContextsMap<CtxDefs>\n        >) => void\n### `microtags/render-support`\n\nThe host-tag builder, prop serializers and attribute escaping that a\ncomponent's static `render` uses. Import it for its side effect:\n\n```ts\nimport 'microtags/render-support'\n```\n\nIt is separate from core so that a client bundle with every\n`.render` link stripped leaves this code out. The `microtags/htm`\ntemplater imports it already, and the [`microtags/build`](#microtagsbuild)\ntransform adds it to any module where it keeps a `.render` link, so\nonly code that calls a `render` static without either needs this\nimport. See\n[ADR-009](./docs/adr/ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md).\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/build`\n\nNode-only. Strips [`.render()`](#builderrenderfn-options) calls from\ndefine chains so the client bundle contains only hydration code.\nRequires `typescript` as a peer dependency.\n\n```ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b761de01-256c-46ce-80ea-a1724a155a95","uuid":"cbb8616a-a3c2-47e0-a548-189c94c49640","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:05:10.455Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### `builder.render(fn, options?)`\n\nAttach a render function that produces the component's inner HTML as a\nstring. The render function receives a context with `props` (plain\nresolved values, not signals), `refs`, `TAG`, `children` (inner HTML\nfrom the caller), and `attrs` (extra attributes from the caller).\n\n```ts\ndefine('my-counter')\n    .withProps(p => ({\n        start: p.number(),\n    }))\n    .withRefs(r => ({\n        display: r.one<HTMLDivElement>(),\n        inc: r.one(),\n        dec: r.one(),\n    }))\n    .render(({ props, refs }) => {\n        return `\n            <div data-ref=\"${refs.display}\">\n                ${props.start}\n            </div>\n            <button data-ref=\"${refs.dec}\">-</button>\n            <button data-ref=\"${refs.inc}\">+</button>\n        `\n    })\n    .setup(ctx => {\n        // hydration code only\n    })\n```\n\nThe returned element class gains two statics: `render(props, options?)`\nwhich returns complete host markup, and `props`, the list of declared\nprop names. `options` accepts `children` (a string of inner HTML) and\n`attrs` (an object of extra attributes, all strings).\n\n`props` are the names declared in `.withProps`. They are serialized onto\nthe host tag with the prop's serializer, so `.setup` can coerce them back\non the client. `attrs` are any other attributes the caller put on the\ntag, such as `class`, `id`, or `aria-*`. They are written to the host tag\nas-is, and are available to the render function so it can forward them\ninside. See [Hydration](#hydration) for an example.\n\nThe static `render` needs the server render support module, which\nbuilds the host tag and serializes props. The `microtags/htm`\ntemplater loads it, on the server and in the browser. Code that calls\na component's `render` static directly, without the templater, must\nimport [`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support) once.\nWithout it, `render` throws an error naming that module.\n\n```ts\nimport 'microtags/render-support'\nimport { MyCounter } from './components.js'\n\nconst markup = MyCounter.render({ start: 5 })\n```\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> This is a breaking change in 0.0.x. Before it, `render` worked with\n> no extra import.\n\nPass `{ client: true }` to keep the render function in the client\nbundle after [`microbuild`](#microbuild) strips it:\n\n```ts\n.render(renderFn, { client: true })\n```\n\nSee [`client:true` vs `--keep`](#clienttrue-vs---keep) for when to\nuse each.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> `.render` on the builder is unrelated to\n> [`microtags/render`](#microtagsrender), which is a DOM reconciler\n> for lists and single items.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n### `builder.setup(ctx)`\n\nRegisters the custom element via `customElements.define` and returns the\nelement class. The returned class exposes `.TAG` and `.refs` as static\nmembers, for use in [serverside rendering](#serverside-example).\n\n```ts\nclass ComponentBuilder {\n    setup (\n        fn:(ctx:SetupContext<\n            Props,\n            RefsMap<RefDefs>,\n            ContextsMap<CtxDefs>\n        >) => void\n### `microtags/render-support`\n\nThe host-tag builder, prop serializers and attribute escaping that a\ncomponent's static `render` uses. Import it for its side effect:\n\n```ts\nimport 'microtags/render-support'\n```\n\nIt is separate from core so that a client bundle with every\n`.render` link stripped leaves this code out. The `microtags/htm`\ntemplater imports it already, and the [`microtags/build`](#microtagsbuild)\ntransform adds it to any module where it keeps a `.render` link, so\nonly code that calls a `render` static without either needs this\nimport. See\n[ADR-009](./docs/adr/ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md).\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/build`\n\nNode-only. Strips [`.render()`](#builderrenderfn-options) calls from\ndefine chains so the client bundle contains only hydration code.\nRequires `typescript` as a peer dependency.\n\n```ts","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JdCrGfdPgWC2VC1aJHwWdd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrrH2R1s2VFRyPLHj68i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014W9AHb1kVEUBxPW77DFBfh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''The returned element class gains two statics: `render(props, options?)`\nwhich returns complete host markup, and `props`, the list of declared\nprop names. `options` accepts `children` (a string of inner HTML) and\n`attrs` (an object of extra attributes, all strings).\n'''\nnew='''The returned element class gains three statics: `render(props,\noptions?)` which returns complete host markup, `renderParts(props,\noptions?)` which returns the same render as parts, and `props`, the list\nof declared prop names. `options` accepts `children` (a string of inner\nHTML) and `attrs` (an object of extra attributes, all strings).\n\n`renderParts` returns `{ tag, attrs, html }`: the host tag name, the\nhost attributes as serialized (not yet escaped) strings, and the inner\nHTML. `attrs` lists the declared props first, then the extra `attrs`,\nskipping prop-only props, null or false values, and extra names that are\nnot valid attribute names. A true boolean is the empty string. Use it to\nbuild the host with another renderer, such as a UI framework, while\n`render` stays the string form:\n\n```ts\nimport 'microtags/render-support'\nimport type { RenderParts } from 'microtags'\n\nconst { tag, attrs, html }:RenderParts = MyCounter.renderParts({\n    start: 5,\n})\n// tag: 'my-counter', attrs: { start: '5' }, html: '<div ...'\n```\n'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nold='''The static `render` needs the server render support module, which\nbuilds the host tag and serializes props.'''\nnew='''The static `render` (and `renderParts`) needs the server render\nsupport module, which builds the host tag and serializes props.'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nold='''Without it, `render` throws an error naming that module.'''\nnew='''Without it, `render` and `renderParts` throw an error naming that\nmodule.'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nold='''The host-tag builder, prop serializers and attribute escaping that a\ncomponent's static `render` uses. Import it for its side effect:'''\nnew='''The host-tag builder, prop serializers and attribute escaping that a\ncomponent's static `render` and `renderParts` use. Import it for its\nside effect:'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nold='''only code that calls a `render` static without either needs this\nimport.'''\nnew='''only code that calls a `render` or `renderParts` static without\neither needs this import.'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='CONTEXT.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''**Markup**:'''\nnew='''**Render parts**:\nThe same server render as the `render` static, split into the host tag\nname, the serialized (unescaped) host attributes, and the inner HTML.\nReturned by the `renderParts` static so another renderer can build the\nhost tag itself.\n_Avoid_: fragments, pieces\n\n**Markup**:'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"README\\|toc\" package.json | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1464,"cache_read_input_tokens":94292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1464},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b761de01-256c-46ce-80ea-a1724a155a95","uuid":"9996286d-fd1a-4af5-9dd9-759693ade17b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:05:19.621Z","request_id":"req_011CgrrH2DMyHZRijneUwsx7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014W9AHb1kVEUBxPW77DFBfh":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).re